        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 67-year-old female patient, admitted on 09/05/2019 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and laboratory workup confirmed an acute exacerbation without signs of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. Pulse oximetry monitoring was performed throughout the stay. Treatment consisted of inhaled bronchodilators via nebulizer, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. The patient responded well to treatment with significant clinical improvement. She is discharged in stable condition on 10/05/2019. I recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close follow-up in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
